WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.290 --> 00:00:04.400
By now, we’re all familiar with the concept
of parallel universes, right?

00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:09.519
In fact, those of you who are familiar with
the SCP Foundation or are maybe even long-time

00:00:09.519 --> 00:00:14.700
fans of the videos on this channel will know
that there are multiple universes that exist

00:00:14.700 --> 00:00:16.450
besides our own.

00:00:16.450 --> 00:00:20.420
There might even be those of you out there
with such refined knowledge that you could

00:00:20.420 --> 00:00:25.630
even name some of the various different universes
and dimensions that the Foundation has come

00:00:25.630 --> 00:00:29.220
into contact with over their years studying
anomalies.

00:00:29.220 --> 00:00:34.841
Today, we’re taking a look at one such anomaly,
an interdimensional wormhole connecting to

00:00:34.841 --> 00:00:42.790
an alternate universe known as SCP-1322, or
by the somewhat questionable nickname, the

00:00:42.790 --> 00:00:44.200
Glory Hole.

00:00:44.200 --> 00:00:49.020
And no, not the one in the airport bathroom
in Minneapolis.

00:00:49.020 --> 00:00:56.850
Let’s take you back to 1952, imagine you’re
a researcher working for the SCP Foundation.

00:00:56.850 --> 00:01:01.890
It’s August, and a new anomaly has been
discovered; it’s a stabilized breach in

00:01:01.890 --> 00:01:07.070
the very fabric of space-time, an aperture
into a completely different universe than

00:01:07.070 --> 00:01:08.680
the one you know.

00:01:08.680 --> 00:01:15.070
A month later, the Foundation has managed
to secure control around this new SCP-1322,

00:01:15.070 --> 00:01:20.950
establishing Site 122 around the breach, given
that this wormhole has a fixed position and

00:01:20.950 --> 00:01:23.000
doesn’t seem to move at all.

00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:27.800
In only another month’s time, you watch
as a metal cylinder one day appears as if

00:01:27.800 --> 00:01:35.799
from nowhere, pushed through SCP-1322 by someone,
or something on the other side.

00:01:35.799 --> 00:01:39.950
Naturally, there’s a buzz among you and
your fellow researchers.

00:01:39.950 --> 00:01:41.190
What is this thing?

00:01:41.190 --> 00:01:42.420
Is it dangerous?

00:01:42.420 --> 00:01:43.710
How did it get here?

00:01:43.710 --> 00:01:49.520
The cylinder is sent off and quarantined,
then sterilized so that it can be safely examined.

00:01:49.520 --> 00:01:54.439
Upon closer examination, it turns out it’s
a hollow container with a screw cap, almost

00:01:54.439 --> 00:01:56.369
like a thermos flask.

00:01:56.369 --> 00:01:57.369
And inside?

00:01:57.369 --> 00:02:02.509
A number of triangular sheets of what appears
to be paper, with strange glyphs written on

00:02:02.509 --> 00:02:03.509
them.

00:02:03.509 --> 00:02:07.600
It’s a message in a bottle, from a completely
separate reality.

00:02:07.600 --> 00:02:12.579
The months go by and experiments involving
SCP-1322 are in full swing.

00:02:12.579 --> 00:02:16.489
But, while you were probably expecting there
to be full-scale explorations through the

00:02:16.489 --> 00:02:21.439
wormhole, your job as a researcher seems to
just be throwing objects attached to rope

00:02:21.439 --> 00:02:22.680
through SCP-1322.

00:02:22.680 --> 00:02:28.689
In fact, the most exciting that those early
experiments got was taking atmosphere samples

00:02:28.689 --> 00:02:30.870
from the other side of the wormhole.

00:02:30.870 --> 00:02:35.269
Even then, you only learn that there’s very
little different about the other dimension’s

00:02:35.269 --> 00:02:39.469
atmosphere when compared to normal Earth levels,
apart from a slightly higher concentration

00:02:39.469 --> 00:02:41.370
of argon in the air.

00:02:41.370 --> 00:02:45.299
Unfortunately, despite even more of the metal
cylinders appearing through the wormhole,

00:02:45.299 --> 00:02:51.090
very little remarkable happens with SCP-1322
over the course of the rest of the year.

00:02:51.090 --> 00:02:57.440
It’s not until July 1953, almost an entire
year after the anomaly was first discovered,

00:02:57.440 --> 00:03:02.279
that the Foundation’s linguistic experts
finally make a breakthrough studying the strange

00:03:02.279 --> 00:03:03.579
glyphic messages.

00:03:03.579 --> 00:03:07.620
The first exciting thing to happen with this
wormhole, and it was some other department

00:03:07.620 --> 00:03:09.169
that uncovered it.

00:03:09.169 --> 00:03:10.219
What a bummer.

00:03:10.219 --> 00:03:15.090
Thanks to the help of their in-house linguistic
and mathematical experts, the Foundation determined

00:03:15.090 --> 00:03:19.859
that the glyphs were some form of cordial,
friendly greeting, but using geometric components

00:03:19.859 --> 00:03:21.809
within written language.

00:03:21.809 --> 00:03:24.540
Imagine if math and written words had a baby.

00:03:24.540 --> 00:03:26.920
No, not your algebra homework.

00:03:26.920 --> 00:03:31.829
Anyway, using the same system of communication,
the Foundation’s linguists sent a reply

00:03:31.829 --> 00:03:36.339
back through SCP-1322 in one of the metal
containers.

00:03:36.339 --> 00:03:39.909
And then… nothing, no more messages.

00:03:39.909 --> 00:03:43.980
For three whole months, the wormhole fell
silent.

00:03:43.980 --> 00:03:48.290
The only thing breaking that lapse in contact
was a light that appeared to activate on the

00:03:48.290 --> 00:03:51.620
far side of SCP-1322.

00:03:51.620 --> 00:03:56.120
Observations revealed that somebody seemed
to have constructed a new containment chamber

00:03:56.120 --> 00:03:58.810
but on the other side of the wormhole.

00:03:58.810 --> 00:04:05.010
In October of 1953, the SCP Foundation finally
began extensive communication with those on

00:04:05.010 --> 00:04:08.239
the opposite side of SCP-1322.

00:04:08.239 --> 00:04:12.459
Through the frequent exchange of written messages,
research teams learned that the glyphs were

00:04:12.459 --> 00:04:17.710
a common system of non-verbal communication
in this alternate universe, a place that soon

00:04:17.710 --> 00:04:24.330
became known as SCP-1322-A. Members of this
dimension’s civilization soon started to

00:04:24.330 --> 00:04:28.770
pick up and incorporate English into their
correspondence with the Foundation, until

00:04:28.770 --> 00:04:33.250
they were eventually able to set up a telegraph,
that used a specially shielded cable running

00:04:33.250 --> 00:04:40.200
through the wormhole, allowing those in dimension
SCP-1322-A to talk to the SCP Foundation on

00:04:40.200 --> 00:04:41.440
the other side.

00:04:41.440 --> 00:04:47.980
The civilization that existed beyond SCP-1322
was apparently a society of human beings,

00:04:47.980 --> 00:04:51.310
almost identical to the people of our own
universe.

00:04:51.310 --> 00:04:55.570
The people that the Foundation was in direct
contact with on the other side were members

00:04:55.570 --> 00:05:00.430
of a scientific organization that had been
tasked with handling the area that surrounded

00:05:00.430 --> 00:05:04.050
SCP-1322 in their universe.

00:05:04.050 --> 00:05:07.810
Not too dissimilar from the Foundation themselves,
by the sound of it.

00:05:07.810 --> 00:05:12.100
However, the biggest dissimilarity between
the inhabitants of each parallel world was

00:05:12.100 --> 00:05:15.730
their different levels of scientific understanding.

00:05:15.730 --> 00:05:16.820
What do we mean by that?

00:05:16.820 --> 00:05:22.250
Well, like many in our universe, the Foundation
scientists on this side had a pretty well-rounded

00:05:22.250 --> 00:05:26.110
and balanced understanding of biology, physics,
and chemistry.

00:05:26.110 --> 00:05:32.560
But those in SCP-1322-A were part of a civilization
that had a far more in-depth understanding

00:05:32.560 --> 00:05:38.200
of only physics, with far less knowledge of
biological science than we might have.

00:05:38.200 --> 00:05:44.010
The SCP-1322-A inhabitants had made many great
strides in the fields of mathematics and high

00:05:44.010 --> 00:05:49.160
energy physics, and this had enabled their
civilization to possess a level of technological

00:05:49.160 --> 00:05:53.950
and engineering sophistication that people
in our world could only dream of.

00:05:53.950 --> 00:05:59.130
And yet, they were hindered by how little
they understood basic biology, such as how

00:05:59.130 --> 00:06:02.360
aspects of nature and human bodies work.

00:06:02.360 --> 00:06:09.140
The people of SCP-1322-A expressed a strong
interest in exchanging samples of music, art,

00:06:09.140 --> 00:06:14.040
literature, and mathematics with the Foundation,
but seemed to have no interest in religion

00:06:14.040 --> 00:06:15.710
or medicine.

00:06:15.710 --> 00:06:21.710
And so the exchange went on, with the denizens
of SCP-1322 sharing detailed records of their

00:06:21.710 --> 00:06:27.250
advanced astronomical observations, encouraging
the Foundation to emulate their deep space

00:06:27.250 --> 00:06:28.250
findings.

00:06:28.250 --> 00:06:32.530
That must’ve been nice, essentially getting
a cheat sheet or a “things to look out for

00:06:32.530 --> 00:06:35.590
in space” guide from an advanced alternate
universe.

00:06:35.590 --> 00:06:40.670
Or, it would have been nice if the data the
Foundation received from the other side actually

00:06:40.670 --> 00:06:43.920
lined up with our own observable universe.

00:06:43.920 --> 00:06:49.370
The Foundation flagged this issue up with
the SCP-1322-A, and they responded by saying

00:06:49.370 --> 00:06:53.500
that personnel should have more candor in
the future if their civilizations were to

00:06:53.500 --> 00:06:56.050
continue sharing scientific findings.

00:06:56.050 --> 00:07:02.500
Needless to say, tensions were beginning to
emerge between these two different universes.

00:07:02.500 --> 00:07:08.350
Following lapses in communication from their
side, the inhabitants of SCP-1322-A reported

00:07:08.350 --> 00:07:12.080
that there had been some form of viral outbreak
in their universe.

00:07:12.080 --> 00:07:16.430
This had seemingly spread from members of
their own organization, infecting the area

00:07:16.430 --> 00:07:22.360
surrounding SCP-1322 and ultimately leading
to the local government imposing quarantine

00:07:22.360 --> 00:07:23.360
measures.

00:07:23.360 --> 00:07:28.960
The Foundation offered to assist, asking for
a sample of this virus, which they then received.

00:07:28.960 --> 00:07:32.920
Analyzing it, they learned it was nothing
more than a harmless variant of the common

00:07:32.920 --> 00:07:37.330
flu, and worked with SCP-1322-A to create
an antidote.

00:07:37.330 --> 00:07:42.490
Now, the flu might not sound all that bad,
but remember, beyond that little wormhole

00:07:42.490 --> 00:07:48.090
was a universe that hadn’t made anywhere
near the advances in biology that we have.

00:07:48.090 --> 00:07:54.280
SCP-1322-A didn’t have vaccines or treatments
to deal with an infection like this, and so

00:07:54.280 --> 00:07:58.620
when this flu virus found itself in their
world - perhaps through a message that was

00:07:58.620 --> 00:08:04.260
passed to them through SCP-1322 - it was able
to cause widespread fatalities.

00:08:04.260 --> 00:08:10.710
Eight million, almost ten whole percent of
SCP-1322-A’s population was killed by the

00:08:10.710 --> 00:08:11.710
outbreak.

00:08:11.710 --> 00:08:15.690
Gradually, however, the Foundation was able
to help them get it under control, but that

00:08:15.690 --> 00:08:18.450
wasn’t the end of their troubles.

00:08:18.450 --> 00:08:25.700
After successfully inoculating their world
against the virus in October 1973, SCP-1322-A

00:08:25.700 --> 00:08:29.550
reported that there had been an unexpected
decrease in pregnancies.

00:08:29.550 --> 00:08:33.529
The following year, the birth rate had dropped
significantly, which was then found to be

00:08:33.529 --> 00:08:40.159
an unexpected side effect of the vaccine the
Foundation had given to SCP-1322-A to stop

00:08:40.159 --> 00:08:41.229
the flu.

00:08:41.229 --> 00:08:46.129
According to them, this had had the knock-on
effect of creating widespread social disorder.

00:08:46.129 --> 00:08:50.850
In January of 1975, when the Foundation once
again offered the people of this alternate

00:08:50.850 --> 00:08:55.390
universe assistance, they were met with the
response “NO THANK YOU.

00:08:55.390 --> 00:08:57.100
YOU HAVE DONE ENOUGH.”

00:08:57.100 --> 00:09:01.779
Later that same year, some new management
assumed control of the organization on the

00:09:01.779 --> 00:09:03.579
other side of the wormhole.

00:09:03.579 --> 00:09:08.600
They maintained an open line of communication
with the Foundation, but in a far more aggressive

00:09:08.600 --> 00:09:12.889
manner, almost as if they were accusing them
of the troubles now faced by their world.

00:09:12.889 --> 00:09:17.709
There was massive upheaval across their globe,
with less than a thousand live births between

00:09:17.709 --> 00:09:20.970
July and September of 1975.

00:09:20.970 --> 00:09:25.720
During that time, the organization refused
to exchange any further scientific or cultural

00:09:25.720 --> 00:09:32.600
information with the Foundation, and eventually,
in October 1975, it severed ties completely.

00:09:32.600 --> 00:09:37.870
They sent a final communication condemning
the SCP Foundation, stating “YOU KILLED

00:09:37.870 --> 00:09:38.870
US.

00:09:38.870 --> 00:09:40.319
YOU DID THIS TO US.

00:09:40.319 --> 00:09:45.160
IN YOUR CARELESSNESS AND YOUR ARROGANCE YOU
HAVE DESTROYED OUR POSTERITY.

00:09:45.160 --> 00:09:46.889
BUT WE SHALL AVENGE.

00:09:46.889 --> 00:09:49.860
WE OF THE LAST GENERATION PLEDGE AND VOW THIS.

00:09:49.860 --> 00:09:52.330
WE WILL FIND A WAY.”

00:09:52.330 --> 00:09:54.019
After that, things were quiet.

00:09:54.019 --> 00:09:59.639
A few stray pathogens made their way through
SCP-1322 but were swiftly destroyed before

00:09:59.639 --> 00:10:00.660
they could spread.

00:10:00.660 --> 00:10:06.720
Then, in January 1977, a high-energy particle
beam was fired through the wormhole at Foundation

00:10:06.720 --> 00:10:07.720
staff.

00:10:07.720 --> 00:10:11.949
It caused minor damage to the containment
chamber, but this was repaired.

00:10:11.949 --> 00:10:16.899
The same thing would happen again in 1984,
a high energy blast this time followed by

00:10:16.899 --> 00:10:20.050
more of the pathogens being sent through the
wormhole.

00:10:20.050 --> 00:10:26.620
And so it went on, every few months the people
of SCP-1322-A would try to attack the Foundation

00:10:26.620 --> 00:10:30.069
like this, and each time the attempt was futile.

00:10:30.069 --> 00:10:36.230
Any damage the beam caused was repaired, and
any pathogens were quickly isolated and destroyed.

00:10:36.230 --> 00:10:41.671
In 1991, the Foundation tried filling the
containment chamber housing SCP-1322 with

00:10:41.671 --> 00:10:45.709
quick setting ceramic, perhaps to bury the
wormhole for good.

00:10:45.709 --> 00:10:50.119
But a month later, their former allies on
the other side released a solvent that ate

00:10:50.119 --> 00:10:51.579
through the ceramic.

00:10:51.579 --> 00:10:56.370
They then tried changing up their tactics,
firing the particle beam still but now also

00:10:56.370 --> 00:11:02.639
beginning to send nanobots, microscopic robots,
through SCP-1322.

00:11:02.639 --> 00:11:06.899
But once again, the Foundation was able to
negate any damage that these devices could

00:11:06.899 --> 00:11:07.980
do.

00:11:07.980 --> 00:11:13.170
These two neighboring universes, home to organizations
that had once tried to share knowledge, were

00:11:13.170 --> 00:11:17.699
now engaged in an endless stalemate, a war
with no winner.

00:11:17.699 --> 00:11:24.040
A device fell through the wormhole in March
1995, which, upon activation, started to heat

00:11:24.040 --> 00:11:28.579
up the atmosphere inside the SCP-1322 containment
chamber.

00:11:28.579 --> 00:11:32.740
The air quickly became superheated plasma,
causing considerable damage until it was then

00:11:32.740 --> 00:11:34.300
vented from the chamber.

00:11:34.300 --> 00:11:39.959
The Foundation had taken their biggest hit
from SCP-1322-A in over a decade and were

00:11:39.959 --> 00:11:45.360
forced to seal the wormhole in altered atmospheric
conditions, keeping it essentially within

00:11:45.360 --> 00:11:49.620
a vacuum, where nothing, not even air, could
exist.

00:11:49.620 --> 00:11:56.209
Three years later, the people of SCP-1322-A
sent another delightful gift to their adversaries:

00:11:56.209 --> 00:11:58.610
a miniature nuclear weapon.

00:11:58.610 --> 00:12:04.420
This almost decimated Site 122, but the damage
was once again repaired and the threat contained.

00:12:04.420 --> 00:12:09.809
Next, in 2006, the residents of the other
universe tried pumping corrosive acid through

00:12:09.809 --> 00:12:15.019
the wormhole, once again causing considerable
damage to the containment chamber on the Foundation’s

00:12:15.019 --> 00:12:16.019
side.

00:12:16.019 --> 00:12:20.399
The following year, the Site 122 Administrator
instructed Foundation personnel to send a

00:12:20.399 --> 00:12:26.189
probe through SCP-1322, perhaps to get a better
idea as to what sort of state the neighboring

00:12:26.189 --> 00:12:28.540
universe was in after all this time.

00:12:28.540 --> 00:12:33.290
A series of eight-kilo iron rods were fired
through the wormhole, however, destroying

00:12:33.290 --> 00:12:39.950
the probe before it could reach SCP-1322-A.
They tried again in 2008, this time with a

00:12:39.950 --> 00:12:46.740
unique gas that rapidly changed into a solid-state
of matter after it passed through SCP-1322.

00:12:46.740 --> 00:12:50.080
This filled the containment chamber, putting
pressure on the structure and threatening

00:12:50.080 --> 00:12:51.889
to tear it apart from the inside.

00:12:51.889 --> 00:12:57.589
Then, the substance condensed after damaging
the SCP-1322 containment chamber, and more

00:12:57.589 --> 00:13:00.259
pathogens and nanobots were introduced.

00:13:00.259 --> 00:13:04.569
The goal was to probably spread them further,
out of the chamber to the outside world, but

00:13:04.569 --> 00:13:07.829
the Foundation was able to prevent this.

00:13:07.829 --> 00:13:13.699
Finally, SCP-1322-A’s last attack involved
a barrage of micro-nuclear warheads, multiple

00:13:13.699 --> 00:13:18.279
high-energy particle beams, and an onslaught
of pathogens and nanobots.

00:13:18.279 --> 00:13:23.569
But, of course, the Foundation had no trouble
containing this attack and repairing the damage

00:13:23.569 --> 00:13:24.569
it caused.

00:13:24.569 --> 00:13:31.529
The story of SCP-1322 is an example of that
old saying: “The road to Hell is paved with

00:13:31.529 --> 00:13:33.019
good intentions.”

00:13:33.019 --> 00:13:38.680
You can start out with a noble goal, say sharing
your scientific knowledge with another universe,

00:13:38.680 --> 00:13:44.110
even helping them cure the flu, but sometimes,
something unforeseen can go wrong and turn

00:13:44.110 --> 00:13:48.269
former friends into bitter, unforgiving enemies.

00:13:48.269 --> 00:13:53.209
These two warring universes are condemned
to continue this sad and deadly dance until

00:13:53.209 --> 00:13:57.679
all the lights go out in one or both of them
forever.

00:13:57.679 --> 00:14:04.721
Now go check out “SCP-001 - The Spiral Path”
and “SCP-173 Origin Story - How 173 Got

00:14:04.721 --> 00:14:09.119
to Site-19” for more sad tales of inevitable
anomalous tragedy!

